<title>MALAYSIA: Chase says in Malaysia-Bahrain consortium.</title>
<headline>Chase says in Malaysia-Bahrain consortium.</headline>
<dateline>KUALA LUMPUR 1997-05-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Malaysian building contractor Chase Perdana Bhd said on Monday it would lead a consortium of Malaysian companies in infrastructure development activities in Bahrain.</p>
<p>In a statement to the Kuala Lumpur Stock Exchange, Chase said it would be involved in construction and infrastructure activities including the &quot;development of the new port and causeway, and oil refinery&quot; in Bahrain.</p>
<p>&quot;The value of the projects discussed are in the region of between US$1.5 billion to $2.0 billion,&quot; said Chase Perdana.</p>
<p>-- Kuala Lumpur newsroom (603-206 2323)</p>
